\label{exer:regular-complete-mealy} We say that a regular language $L \subseteq A^*$ is \emph{regular-complete under Mealy reductions} if for every regular language $K \subseteq B^*$, there exists a "Mealy machine" $f : B^* \to A^*$ such that 
